                    <div class="faqquestionWrap mb30 active" data-rel="tab-a-1">
                        <div class="left">
                            <p class="faqHeading"> How is AI transforming the purpose of GCCs?</p>

                            <img src="https://images.mastersunion.link/uploads/23052025/v1/Group35539.svg"
                                class="toggler" alt="">
                        </div>
                        <p class="faqanswer" id="tab-a-1"> AI is shifting GCCs from cost-focused back offices to
                            AI-native value creators. Instead of labor arbitrage, they now drive cognitive arbitrage by
                            generating revenue, improving outcomes, building IP, and using predictive intelligence to
                            proactively optimize supply chains, risk, operations, and enterprise-wide decision-making.
                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="faqquestionWrap mb30 " data-rel="tab-a-2">
                        <div class="left">
                            <p class="faqHeading"> What is Agentic AI and why is it important for GCCs in 2026?</p>

                            <img src="https://images.mastersunion.link/uploads/23052025/v1/Group35539.svg"
                                class="toggler" alt="">
                        </div>
                        <p class="faqanswer" id="tab-a-2"> Agentic AI goes beyond prompt-based GenAI by autonomously
                            planning, reasoning, and executing multi-step workflows. For GCCs, it enables end-to-end
                            automation across IT, HR, and finance, creating a 24/7 digital workforce that reduces manual
                            intervention and accelerates enterprise scalability.
                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="faqquestionWrap mb30 " data-rel="tab-a-3">
                        <div class="left">
                            <p class="faqHeading">What are the key AI use cases in modern GCCs?</p>

                            <img src="https://images.mastersunion.link/uploads/23052025/v1/Group35539.svg"
                                class="toggler" alt="">
                        </div>
                        <p class="faqanswer" id="tab-a-3">AI powers finance automation, fraud detection, intelligent
                            hiring, attrition prediction, AI-led HR helpdesks, code generation, predictive maintenance,
                            self-healing IT systems, and advanced customer support bots by improving productivity,
                            reducing costs, and increasing operational velocity across enterprise functions.
                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="faqquestionWrap mb30 " data-rel="tab-a-4">
                        <div class="left">
                            <p class="faqHeading"> What are the major challenges in AI adoption?

                            </p>

                            <img src="https://images.mastersunion.link/uploads/23052025/v1/Group35539.svg"
                                class="toggler" alt="">
                        </div>
                        <p class="faqanswer" id="tab-a-4"> The biggest barriers are talent shortages, unclear ROI, weak
                            strategic alignment, legacy infrastructure, and organizational resistance. Many AI pilots
                            fail to scale due to limited AI literacy, lack of executive sponsorship, and outdated
                            systems that restrict seamless AI integration.

                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="faqquestionWrap mb30 " data-rel="tab-a-5">
                        <div class="left">
                            <p class="faqHeading"> How should GCCs address the AI talent challenge?

                            </p>

                            <img src="https://images.mastersunion.link/uploads/23052025/v1/Group35539.svg"
                                class="toggler" alt="">
                        </div>
                        <p class="faqanswer" id="tab-a-5">
                             GCCs must upskill teams from process execution to AI governance, while hiring for emerging roles like AI strategists, ML engineers, AI product managers, and ethics leaders. Building AI-first career paths ensures long-term capability development and competitive advantage.

                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="faqquestionWrap mb30 " data-rel="tab-a-6">
                        <div class="left">
                            <p class="faqHeading">  What is the future of AI-driven GCCs by 2030?

                            </p>

                            <img src="https://images.mastersunion.link/uploads/23052025/v1/Group35539.svg"
                                class="toggler" alt="">
                        </div>
                        <p class="faqanswer" id="tab-a-6"> By 2030, GCCs will operate as AI-native hubs running hyper-automated operations with embedded governance. They will shift from service providers to enterprise innovation engines, driving R&D, autonomous decision-making, and responsible AI frameworks at global scale.
                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="faqquestionWrap mb30 " data-rel="tab-a-7">
                        <div class="left">
                            <p class="faqHeading">Will the Executive Leadership Programme in AI & GCC Transformation be online or offline? </p>

                            <img src="https://images.mastersunion.link/uploads/23052025/v1/Group35539.svg"
                                class="toggler" alt="">
                        </div>

                        <div class="faqanswer" id="tab-a-7">The classes will be hybrid where learners can choose their preference to join online or offline.
                        </div>

